  3.784152176275079*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fbb3bea0-e7c9-4e71-8189-\
0c39bb6e2333"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A static nonlinearity (e.g., cuber, hard limiter, etc) followed by a linear \
dynamic subsystem is called a Hammerstein system after the German \
mathematician Adolf Hammerstein (if you can read German see ",
 ButtonBox["https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Hammerstein",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Hammerstein"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Hammerstein"],
 ") who studied such systems."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.783700018028175*^9, 3.783700163503906*^9}, {
  3.7837126965203156`*^9, 3.783712709486042*^9}, {3.784152185306183*^9, 
