Cell[TextData[{
 "This discovery function returns suitable static models together with a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Score\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and a measure of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Complexity\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. A \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]good\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] model is one which has a \
high Score (a good fit) but a low level of complexity under the assumption \
that simplicity is important. Using these two criteria we choose the p1 uu + \
p2 ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["uu", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7174c3bb-4c3e-4aca-9cdc-a5ee99e5b8fc"],
 " model. This model form is exactly the static nonlinearity used in the \
Hammerstein model. Furthermore  the two parameters of this model are p1 = 0.1 \
and p2 = 0.1 are has a value near to 10 which is the same as that used when \
the Wiener system was specified. In other words we have identified the static \
nonlinearity."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7840551170974817`*^9, 3.784055361486759*^9}, {
  3.784055440114767*^9, 3.78405552007748*^9}, {3.784055571865853*^9, 
  3.784055627242165*^9}, {3.784055660406129*^9, 3.7840556812183466`*^9}, {
  3.784055752246482*^9, 3.784055810822974*^9}, {3.784766100188249*^9, 
  3.784766229674331*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"74d8de1d-effd-431a-8d6b-\
99b1b93e8a26"],

Cell["\<\
FindFormula does a quick fit and test of a wide range of functions. Lets redo \
the fit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.784413758414238*^9, 3.7844138317129536`*^9}, 
   3.784766245820609*^9},ExpressionUUID->"08a96f85-d9d0-41fe-bd61-\
efcef42496d2"],

